_⚠️ Potential issue_ | _🟡 Minor_

**Invite-list fetch errors are silently swallowed — user sees a misleading empty state.**

When `fetchInvitesForItem` fails on tab open, only `console.error` is called. The UI falls through to `invites.length === 0` and renders `"no active invite links"`, which is indistinguishable from a genuine empty list.

<details>
<summary>🛠️ Proposed fix</summary>

```diff
   .catch((err) => {
     if (!cancelled) {
       console.error('Failed to fetch invites:', err);
+      setError('failed to load invite links');
     }
   })
```
</details>

<!-- suggestion_start -->

<details>
<summary>📝 Committable suggestion</summary>

> ‼️ **IMPORTANT**
> Carefully review the code before committing. Ensure that it accurately replaces the highlighted code, contains no missing lines, and has no issues with indentation. Thoroughly test & benchmark the code to ensure it meets the requirements.

```suggestion
    fetchInvitesForItem(ipnsName)
      .then((result) => {
        if (!cancelled) {
          setInvites(result);
        }
      })
      .catch((err) => {
        if (!cancelled) {
          console.error('Failed to fetch invites:', err);
          setError('failed to load invite links');
        }
      })
      .finally(() => {
        if (!cancelled) {
          setInvitesLoading(false);
        }
      });
```

</details>

<!-- suggestion_end -->

<details>
<summary>🤖 Prompt for AI Agents</summary>

```
Verify each finding against the current code and only fix it if needed.

In `@apps/web/src/components/file-browser/InviteLinkTab.tsx` around lines 48 - 63,
The fetchInvitesForItem call currently only logs errors so the UI shows a
misleading empty list; modify the component to track fetch errors (e.g., add an
invitesError state) and in the .catch handler set that error (instead of only
console.error) while still respecting the cancelled flag, ensure
setInvitesLoading(false) remains in .finally, and update the UI rendering logic
to show an error state/message (or toast) when invitesError is set rather than
rendering "no active invite links"; reference fetchInvitesForItem, setInvites,
setInvitesLoading, and the invites state when making these changes.
```

</details>

